  "body": "Fork synced at v0.18.0 (branch cut from upstream/main 3e9b8ae1).\n\n## What changed\n`ImportTools` gains an explicit `ImportMode` (`ImportTools::with_mode`; `new` = Add, so existing behaviour and tests hold):\n- **Add** (default): skip identical, rename a different duplicate to `Name (2)`.\n- **Update**: a same-named tool takes the imported definition in place (same entity, controller number kept, operations using it read Stale); identical skipped; unmatched names added.\n- **Replace**: Update, and document tools the library lacks are removed. If an operation uses such a tool the whole import is refused by tool and operation name, nothing applied.\nUpdate/Replace run the `ChangeTool` gates (torch, retype stranding an op, body/cutter fit) and refuse a name that is not a tool. One undo unit (removal uses the `DeleteTool` snapshot, so undo restores number/body/cutter). `ImportReport` gains `updated`/`replaced`/`removed`. GUI: a mode combo beside \"Import library...\"; `cam.importTools(path, mode?)` and MCP `import_tool_library` take `mode` (cam.d.ts updated). Key is the tool name; #898's part number is the intended future key (decision file `docs/decisions/899-tool-import-modes.md`).\n\n## Tested\n`cargo test -p camcraft-app --test tool_import_modes` (9: update in place + identity/number/Stale/undo/redo, update add+skip, nothing-to-do, non-tool name refusal, retype refusal, replace remove + undo exact, replace refusal when an op uses a tool, Add default unchanged, mode parse), `--test tool_library`, `--test mcp` (new `tool_library_import_modes_update_and_replace_over_mcp`), `--test scripting`. `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings` clean. Quick gate: ui suites ok; app suites failed only `scripting` (cam.d.ts drift, fixed and re-run green).\n\n## Not exercised\nThe GUI combo is not covered by a structural assertion (no existing assertion covers the page's import row); no snapshot PNGs touched. Full quick gate not re-run after the d.ts/lint fix (affected suites re-run individually).\n\nChangelog: Tool library import has Add / Update / Replace modes: update a same-named tool in place (operations go Stale) or replace the library, refusing to remove a tool an operation uses (#899, PR #1060)\nEffort: medium\n\nFixes #899\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
